(Developer notes)

Docker images (see README for details). The engine comes from a galileo checkout next to this one:
>docker build --build-context galileo=../galileo -t cascala/igalileo:0.3.0 -t cascala/igalileo:latest .
>docker push cascala/igalileo:0.3.0 && docker push cascala/igalileo:latest

Multi-architecture (Intel and Apple Silicon) in one go:
>docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64 --build-context galileo=../galileo \
   -t cascala/igalileo:0.3.0 -t cascala/igalileo:latest --push .

Keep the old version tags (0.2.0, 0.2.1): they are the Scala/JVM kernel.

Execute the example notebooks with a local image before committing them:
>IGALILEO_IMAGE=cascala/igalileo:0.3.0 examples/src/execute.sh examples/*.ipynb examples/*/*.ipynb
